{
  "_notes": [
    "PROJECT EVE HUMAN EVENT CONSEQUENCE RULES.",
    "HumanEventEngine decides what the NPC does. HumanEventConsequenceRouter decides which Project Eve systems must change because it happened.",
    "The router does NOT invent missing facts such as stolen amount, medical diagnosis, pregnancy outcome, legal charge, or job termination reason.",
    "If a consequence needs information the world has not supplied, it is queued for the owning system instead of guessed.",
    "All Human Event Domains are covered through domainDefaults. eventOverrides only add special handling.",
    "Relationship changes happen immediately only when the target is aware of the event. Hidden acts such as cheating or secret betrayal use deferred consequences until discovery.",
    "Major events request memory/history and force a deep update, regardless of Tier 1-4 background timer."
  ],
